      "decoratedLyrics": "[Genre: Industrial Dark Americana]\n[Mood: Ominous, Heavy, Cinematic, Dystopian]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Weary | Prophet-like]\n[Instrumentation: Detuned Banjo, Industrial Drone, Sub-bass pulse, Metallic percussion]\n[Tempo: Slow | Deliberate]\n[Intro]\n[Instrumental: A single, detuned banjo plays a stark, repetitive riff. Dry and lonely.]\n[Soundscape: A low-frequency hum begins to fade in, very subtle at first.]\n[Verse 1]\n[Vocal Delivery: Spoken word | Stoic]\nIt started as a trickle, just a leak in the dam\nNow it’s a river of red ink, drowning the land\nWe printed the paper, we signed the decree\nWe spent the tomorrow of the brave and the free.\n[Pre-Chorus]\n[The industrial hum gets louder, turning into a rhythmic throbbing]\n[Vocal Style: Gritty | Resonant]\nThirty-three percent comes due in a year\n[spoken] That’s the maturity wall.\nThe reeFynancing risk is the thing that you fear\nThe clock on the wall doesn't tick, it just falls.\n[Chorus]\n[Instrumentation: The Banjo is now fighting against a wall of Sub-bass noise]\n[Vocal Emotion: Haunting | Powerful]\nThirty-eight trillion ghosts standing in line\nBorn with a debt they didn't ask to sign\nWe counted the stars and we sold the sky\nNow the numbers are too heavy to fly\nYeah, the numbers are too heavy to fly.\n[Interlude]\n[Industrial Drone swells | Metallic clanging sounds like a debt clock ticking]\n[The Banjo plays frantically but is buried in the mix]\n[Verse 2]\n[Vocal Delivery: Cynical | Dark]\nFive zero point seven percent in notes\n[spoken] That’s the intermediate term.\nWe’re feeding the fire with the wooden boats\nAnd the bond market twists like a dying worm.\nNinety-seven-zero billion just to pay the rent\nOn the money we borrowed and the money we spent.\n[Bridge]\n[Tempo: Dragging | Heavy]\n[Vocal Style: Whisper to Shout]\nIt ain't a policy.\nIt ain't a mistake.\nIt's a Lean on the baby for the grandfather's sake!\n[shouted] For the grandfather's sake!\n[Chorus]\n[Full Industrial Noise | The Banjo is barely audible]\nThirty-eight trillion ghosts standing in line\nBorn with a debt they didn't ask to sign\nWe counted the stars and we sold the sky\nNow the numbers are too heavy to fly.\n[Outro]\n[The music cuts out abruptly]\n[Silence for 2 seconds]\n[Vocal: Acapella | Whisper]\nToo heavy to fly.\n[End]",
