      "decoratedLyrics": "[Genre: Industrial Dark Waltz]\n[Mood: Satirical, Twisted, Drunken, Dissonant]\n[Vocalist: Male (Lead) | Baritone | Theatrical | Ringmaster style]\n[Vocalist: Female (Harmony) | Soprano | Ethereal | Haunting]\n[Instrumentation: Solo Cello, Out-of-tune Upright Piano, 3/4 Percussion, Clanking Glasses]\n[Tempo: 3/4 Time | Moderate Waltz]\n[Intro]\n[Instrumental: A clean, classical Cello plays a graceful waltz melody in 3/4 time.]\n[Soundscape: The faint sound of a cocktail party, clinking glass, polite laughter.]\n[Verse 1]\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: Smooth | Aristocratic]\nThe printer hums a melody, a secret little tune\nThe first sip is the sweetest, beneath the silver moon.\nWe catch the water early, while the river is still clear\nBefore the mud can muddy it, before the price is dear.\nWe buy the land, we buy the gold, we buy the stock and bond\nWith magic paper money from the magic little pond.\n[Chorus]\n[Rhythm: Strong Waltz Beat | ONE-two-three, ONE-two-three]\n[Vocalist: Male & Female Duet]\n[Male: Boisterous | Female: Operatic High Harmony]\nSo dance, dance, the Cantillon Waltz\nThe money is real but the value is false!\n[Female Vocal: Ooooooh-aaahhhhh (Siren call)]\nIt flows from the top, shiny and new\nBy the time it gets down, there’s nothing for you.\nRound and round the table goes\nWhere the money stops, nobody knows.\n[Interlude]\n[Instrumental: The Cello melody begins to waver. Pitch shifting. Sounds slightly \"drunk\".]\n[Instrumentation: Add Industrial scrape]\n[Verse 2]\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: Mocking | Darker]\nDown in the valley where the shadows grow tall\nThe shopkeeper waits for the water to fall.\nBut the river is thick with the dirt and the dust\nThe bread costs a dollar, but you pay with a crust.\n[spoken] You see, prices rise before the wages do.\nThe rich get the asset, the poor get the due.\nA hidden tax on the man with the plow\nWhile the banker is wiping the sweat from his brow.\n[Bridge]\n[Tempo: Slowing down | Dragging]\n[Effect: Heavy Tape Saturation | Warped Audio]\n[Vocalist: Male with Female Whisper layers]\nThe wine turns to vinegar.\nThe gold turns to led.\nYou’re working for paper that’s already dead.\n[Male Shouted] It's already dead!\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Instrumental: A chaotic, dissonant acoustic guitar solo over a distorted waltz beat. Sounds like the band is falling down the stairs.]\n[Chorus]\n[Full Industrial Noise | The Waltz beat is heavy and mechanical]\n[Vocalist: Male & Female Duet]\nSo dance, dance, the Cantillon Waltz\nThe money is real but the value is false!\n[Female Vocal: High, distorted wail]\nIt flows from the top, shiny and new\nBy the time it gets down, there’s nothing for you.\n[Outro]\n[Tempo: Accelerating | Frantic]\nRound and round!\nThe value is false!\n[Vocalist: Female (Whisper)] Keep dancing.\n[Instrumental: The cello snaps a string. Abrupt silence.]\n[End]",
