      "summary": "\"Defense of Nothing\" is a driving, aggressive track that highlights a critical turning point in the nation's decline: the moment when the cost of paying for the past (interest on debt) exceeds the cost of defending the present (the military budget)3. The song uses tribal, tom-heavy drumming to mimic a war march, but the lyrics reveal a hollow army. It depicts a nation that is \"cannibalizing\" itself, spending more to feed the bond market than to protect its own borders or citizens4.",
      "decoratedLyrics": "[Genre: Industrial Dark Americana, Tribal Folk Rock]\n[Mood: Aggressive, Urgent, Tribal, Militant]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Shouted | Commanding]\n[Instrumentation: Heavy Tom Drums, Distorted Acoustic Guitar, Aggressive Strumming, Metallic Percussion]\n[Tempo: Fast | Driving | 4/4 Stomp]\n[Intro]\n[Instrumental: Thunderous, tribal tom-tom drums beating a war rhythm. Aggressive acoustic guitar strumming enters.]\n[Soundscape: Distant sirens mixed with the sound of marching boots.]\n[Verse 1]\n[Vocal Delivery: Urgent | Gritty]\nThe General is waiting on a check that never comes\nWe sold the ammunition just to buy the marching drums.\nThe border is a line drawn in the shifting sand\nWe mortgaged off the castle to secure the land.\nThey say we need a fighter, they say we need a wall\nBut the banker owns the brick, and the banker owns the hall.\n[Chorus]\n[Rhythm: Heavy Stomp | BOOM-clap-BOOM-clap]\n[Vocal Style: Shouted Anthem]\nThe shield is rusted, the sword is sold!\nWe pay the interest in blood and gold.\nNine-Seven-Zero Bill-yun just to keep the lights on low\n[spoken] That’s more than the army.\nWe’re guarding the vault where the nothing grows.\nDefense of nothing!\nDefense of nothing!\n[Instrumental Break]\n[Instrumentation: Distorted Harmonica solo over heavy drums]\n[Verse 2]\n[Vocal Delivery: Cynical | Spoken word to shout]\nWe crossed the Rubicon in twenty-twenty-five\nKeeping the debt dead, just to keep the lie alive.\nThe sick are waiting in the hallway for a bed\n[spoken] But we paid the bondholder instead.\nThe parasite is hungry, it’s growing in the chest\nIt eats the host alive, and it never takes a rest.\n[Bridge]\n[Tempo: Half-time | Heavy]\n[Vocal Style: Growling | Menacing]\nNineteen percent of the revenue stream.\n[spoken] Gone.\nInto the hole of the fever dream.\nWe don't pay for safety.\nWe don't pay for health.\nWe only pay the rent on the phantom wealth.\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Instrumental: Frantic, percussive acoustic guitar solo. Fast strumming. High energy.]\n[Chorus]\n[Full Industrial Noise | Maximum Volume]\nThe shield is rusted, the sword is sold!\nWe pay the interest in blood and gold.\nNine-Seven-Zero Bill-yun just to keep the lights on low\nWe’re guarding the vault where the nothing grows.\nDefense of nothing!\n[Outro]\n[Tempo: Relentless Drumming]\n[Vocal: Chanted]\nFeed the bond!\nFeed the bond!\nStarve the man!\n[spoken] Defense of nothing.\n[End]",
      "cleanLyrics": "[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nThe General is waiting on a check that never comes\nWe sold the ammunition just to buy the marching drums.\nThe border is a line drawn in the shifting sand\nWe mortgaged off the castle to secure the land.\nThey say we need a fighter, they say we need a wall\nBut the banker owns the brick, and the banker owns the hall.\n[Chorus]\nThe shield is rusted, the sword is sold!\nWe pay the interest in blood and gold.\nNine-Seven-Zero Billion just to keep the lights on low\nThat’s more than the army.\nWe’re guarding the vault where the nothing grows.\nDefense of nothing!\nDefense of nothing!\n[Instrumental Break]\n[Verse 2]\nWe crossed the Rubicon in twenty-twenty-five\nKeeping the debt dead, just to keep the lie alive.\nThe sick are waiting in the hallway for a bed\nBut we paid the bondholder instead.\nThe parasite is hungry, it’s growing in the chest\nIt eats the host alive, and it never takes a rest.\n[Bridge]\nNineteen percent of the revenue stream.\nGone.\nInto the hole of the fever dream.\nWe don't pay for safety.\nWe don't pay for health.\nWe only pay the rent on the phantom wealth.\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Chorus]\nThe shield is rusted, the sword is sold!\nWe pay the interest in blood and gold.\nNine-Seven-Zero Billion just to keep the lights on low\nWe’re guarding the vault where the nothing grows.\nDefense of nothing!\n[Outro]\nFeed the bond!\nFeed the bond!\nStarve the man!\nDefense of nothing.\n© 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
