      "leadArchetype": "The Indentured (BNPL Youth)",
      "summary": "\"Pay in Four (Invisible Chains)\" captures the high-speed, low-grade panic of the modern consumer. It follows \"Jenny,\" who owns nothing but rents everything through \"four easy payments.\" The song explores the \"Invisible Debt\" —micro-liabilities that clutter the mind like digital shrapnel. Musically, it juxtaposes a frantic, fast-picked acoustic guitar against glitchy, electronic percussion, mimicking the constant buzzing of payment reminders on a smartphone .",
      "decoratedLyrics": "[Genre: Industrial Dark Americana, Glitch Folk]\n[Mood: Nervous, Frantic, Anxious, Paranoia]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Rapid-fire | Tense]\n[Instrumentation: Fast Acoustic Picking, Glitchy Electronic Beats, Cell Phone Vibration Samples, Distorted Bass]\n[Tempo: Fast | Rushed | Heartbeat pace]\n[Intro]\n[Instrumental: A rapid, nervous acoustic guitar riff. Clean but very fast.]\n[Soundscape: The sound of digital notifications (beeps/buzzes) rhythmically integrated into the beat.]\n[Verse 1]\n[Vocal Delivery: Fast | Breathless]\nJenny’s got a dress for the Friday night\nShe didn't have the cash but the fit was right.\nClick the little button, scan the little face\nEnter the number, join the race.\nIt’s only twenty dollars, that ain't a lot\nUntil you add the other fifty things she bought.\nThe shoes, the phone, the meal, the rent\nShe doesn't know where the money went.\n[Pre-Chorus]\n[Rhythm: Stuttering | Glitchy]\n[Vocal Style: Whispered to Shouted]\nDing. Buzz. Flash. Ring.\nYou don't own a single thing.\nThe algo-rhythm knows your name\nIt feeds you to the hunger game.\n[Chorus]\n[Instrumentation: Heavy, driving bass enters. Chaotic.]\n[Vocal Emotion: Panic | Manic]\nQuarter now, quarter then!\nQuarter when I'm dead, Amen!\nFour easy payments to sell your soul\nDigging a thousand shallow holes.\nI got a thousand little cuts inside my head\nAnd a subscription to the very bed!\n[shouted] The very bed I sleep in!\n[Interlude]\n[Instrumental: The acoustic guitar loops and glitches, skipping like a broken CD. Electronic noise rises.]\n[Verse 2]\n[Vocal Delivery: Cynical | Observant]\nShe’s working three gigs just to pay the app\nRunning on a wheel in a velvet trap.\nSixty percent buy what they can't afford\n[spoken] Praying to the digital lord.\nDelinquency rising on the younger side\nNowhere to run and nowhere to hide.\nThe notification is a bayonet\nSticking in the side of the internet.\n[Bridge]\n[Tempo: Halftime breakdown | Disoriented]\n[Vocal Style: Distorted | Robotized]\nYour payment is processed.\nYour payment is due.\nYour payment is late.\nWe are coming for you.\n[Tempo: Ramps back up to maximum speed]\n[shouted] We are coming for you!\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Instrumental: Frenetic acoustic shredding mixed with industrial static. Sounds like a panic attack.]\n[Chorus]\n[Full Volume | High Anxiety]\nQuarter now, quarter then!\nQuarter when I'm dead, Amen!\nFour easy payments to sell your soul\nDigging a thousand shallow holes.\nI got a thousand little cuts inside my head\nAnd a subscription to the very bed!\n[Outro]\n[Rhythm: Abrupt stops and starts]\nPay in four.\nPay in four.\nPay in...\n[Sound: A loud digital \"error\" tone]\n[Silence]\n[End]",
      "cleanLyrics": "[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nJenny’s got a dress for the Friday night\nShe didn't have the cash but the fit was right.\nClick the little button, scan the little face\nEnter the number, join the race.\nIt’s only twenty dollars, that ain't a lot\nUntil you add the other fifty things she bought.\nThe shoes, the phone, the meal, the rent\nShe doesn't know where the money went.\n[Pre-Chorus]\nDing. Buzz. Flash. Ring.\nYou don't own a single thing.\nThe algorithm knows your name\nIt feeds you to the hunger game.\n[Chorus]\nQuarter now, quarter then!\nQuarter when I'm dead, Amen!\nFour easy payments to sell your soul\nDigging a thousand shallow holes.\nI got a thousand little cuts inside my head\nAnd a subscription to the very bed!\nThe very bed I sleep in!\n[Interlude]\n[Verse 2]\nShe’s working three gigs just to pay the app\nRunning on a wheel in a velvet trap.\nSixty percent buy what they can't afford\nPraying to the digital lord.\nDelinquency rising on the younger side\nNowhere to run and nowhere to hide.\nThe notification is a bayonet\nSticking in the side of the internet.\n[Bridge]\nYour payment is processed.\nYour payment is due.\nYour payment is late.\nWe are coming for you.\nWe are coming for you!\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Chorus]\nQuarter now, quarter then!\nQuarter when I'm dead, Amen!\nFour easy payments to sell your soul\nDigging a thousand shallow holes.\nI got a thousand little cuts inside my head\nAnd a subscription to the very bed!\n[Outro]\nPay in four.\nPay in four.\nPay in...\n(Error Tone)\n© 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
      "musicalPrompt": "[Genre: Industrial Dark Americana]\n[Style: Glitch Folk]\n[Mood: Nervous, Frantic, Anxious, Paranoia]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Rapid-fire Delivery | Tense]\n[Instrumentation: Fast Acoustic Guitar Picking, Electronic Glitch Percussion, Distorted Bass, Digital Noise]\n[Production: Chopped, Stuttering Effects, High BPM]\n[Structure: Relentless pace, Sudden stops]",
