      "cleanLyrics": "[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nIt was quiet on the surface, the water was still\nWe paid the interest with a shiny new bill.\nThe Hedge was safe, the crash flow was green\nWe oiled the gears of the money machine.\nBut stability is a liar, stability is a ghost\nIt invites the devil to become the host.\nWe took the leverage, we took the bet\nWe haven't seen the bottom of the ocean yet.\n[Pre-Chorus]\nBorrow to pay the principal!\nThat was last year.\nBorrow to pay the interest!\nThat is right now.\nThe Ponzi stage is the final bow.\nThe final bow!\n[Chorus]\nThe long calm ends, the wave attacks!\nThe floor is gone, the ceiling cracks!\nMinsky’s Moment is at the door\nHe isn't asking for a little, he's taking it all!\nLiquidity is a ghost in the hall\nWatch the tower shake and fall!\n[Interlude]\n[Verse 2]\nSell the asset! Sell the farm!\nRing the bell! Sound the alarm!\nThere are no buyers, the book is closed\nThe emperor is naked and completely exposed.\nThe margin call is a telephone wire\nStrangling the neck of the buyer and the liar.\nTwelve-zero percent of the G-D-P\nCollapsing in a wave of the rising sea.\n[Bridge]\nPanic.\nSell.\nPanic.\nSell.\nPanic.\nSell.\nRUN!\n[Guitar Solo]\n[Chorus]\nThe long calm ends, the wave attacks!\nThe floor is gone, the ceiling cracks!\nMinsky’s Moment is at the door\nHe isn't asking for a little, he's taking it all!\nWatch the tower shake and fall!\n[Outro]\nIt's coming down!\nIt's coming down!\nIt's coming...\n(Silence)\n© 2025 The Shady River Bard. All rights reserved.",
      "musicalPrompt": "[Genre: Industrial Noise Rock]\n[Style: Avant-Garde Metal]\n[Mood: Chaotic, Panicked, Manic, Violent]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Shouting | Unhinged]\n[Instrumentation: Distorted Bass, Screaming Feedback, Polyrhythmic Drums, Air Raid Siren, Wall of Sound]\n[Production: Red-lining, Distorted, High Contrast]\n[Structure: Accelerating Tempo, Abrupt Ending]",
      "artPrompt": "A high-speed, blurred black-and-white photograph of a man in a business suit falling backwards off a steel beam. He is screaming. Below him, instead of a street, is a gaping mouth of jagged, rusted metal gears. High contrast, motion blur, terrifying perspective. --ar 9:16\nThis is the terrifying heart of the album’s economic philosophy. Track 8 isn't just a chaotic noise track; it is a direct translation of Hyman Minsky’s Financial Instability Hypothesis.\nFor decades, mainstream economists ignored Minsky because his math was \"messy\" and he argued that the free market is inherently unstable. After the 2008 crash, everyone suddenly knew his name.\nHere is the breakdown of the theory that drives the song.\n1. The Core Thesis: \"Stability Breeds Instability\"\nMinsky’s most profound insight was that stability is dangerous.1\nWhen the economy is stable (the \"Great Moderation\"), banks and borrowers feel safe.\nBecause they feel safe, they take on more risk to get higher returns.2\nOver time, this risk-taking transforms a stable economy into a fragile one.\nTherefore, a crash isn't caused by an external shock (like a war or a plague); it is generated internally by the very success of the system.3\n2. The Three Stages of Debt (The Descent)\nMinsky categorized borrowers into three stages. Track 8 follows this progression linearly.\nStage 1: Hedge Finance (The Safe Zone)\nDefinition: The borrower has enough cash flow to pay back both the interest and the principal on their loan.\nLyric: \"The Hedge was safe, the cash flow was green.\"\nStatus: Sustainable.\nStage 2: Speculative Finance ( The Slippery Slope)\nDefinition: The borrower has enough cash flow to pay the interest, but not the principal. They must \"roll over\" the debt (borrow new money to pay off the old loan) constantly.4 They are betting that banks will always lend to them.\nLyric: \"Borrow to pay the principal / That was last year.\"\nStatus: Vulnerable to rising interest rates.\nStage 3: Ponzi Finance (The Death Spiral)\nDefinition: The borrower has no cash flow to pay the principal or the interest. They are borrowing money just to pay the interest on previous loans. They are alive only because the value of the asset (house, stock, crypto) keeps going up. If the asset price stops rising, they are instantly bankrupt.\nLyric: \"Borrow to pay the interest / That is right now / The Ponzi stage is the final bow.\"\nStatus: Doomed.\n3. The \"Minsky Moment\"\nThis is the moment the music stops.\nEventually, the debt load gets too heavy, or interest rates rise slightly. The \"Ponzi\" borrowers can no longer borrow enough to pay their interest.5 They are forced to sell their assets (houses, stocks) to get cash.\nThe Panic: When everyone sells at once to pay debts, asset prices crash.\nThe Collapse: Because the asset prices crash, the \"Speculative\" borrowers (who relied on rolling over debt) now look insolvent, so banks cut them off too.6\nThe Result: The entire system implodes in a self-reinforcing downward spiral. This is the \"Liquidity is a ghost in the hall\" line—suddenly, there is no money anywhere.\n4. Why It Fits \"The Shady River\"\nIn the context of the album, we are arguing that the entire US economy has moved into the Ponzi Finance stage.\nThe government borrows money just to pay the interest on its debt.\nZombie companies (companies that don't make profit) stay alive only by cheap loans.\nThe song ends with silence because, in a Minsky Moment, credit—the lifeblood of the economy—simply vanishes."
