      "musicalPrompt": "[Genre: Southern Rock]\n[Style: Soulful Anthem]\n[Mood: Determined, Gritty, Hopeful, Strong]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Raspy Soul]\n[Instrumentation: Acoustic Guitar intro, Hammond B3 Organ, Slide Guitar, Heavy Kick Drum, Choir Backing]\n[Production: Warm, analog, building dynamic range]\n[Structure: Slow start, anthemic climax, rhythmic outro]",
      "artPrompt": "A close-up, ground-level shot of a pair of worn leather work boots standing on solid granite rock. In the background, out of focus, a city made of playing cards is collapsing. The sun is rising behind the boots, casting a long, golden shadow. --ar 1:1\nUnderstanding the Economics: \"Creative Destruction\"\nThis song embodies the concept of Schumpeter’s Gale or Creative Destruction.\nThe Theory: Joseph Schumpeter argued that economic progress requires the destruction of the old, inefficient structures to make way for the new. The \"pain\" of the crash is actually the system healing itself, flushing out the \"malinvestment\" (the rot).\nPrice vs. Value: The song draws a hard line between Price (what the market says something is worth in dollars) and Value (the utility and scarcity of the actual thing). During a hyper-inflationary or deflationary event, Price becomes meaningless (volatile), but Value remains constant.\n\"Immutable\": The Bridge introduces this word deliberately. It is a keyword for Blockchain/Bitcoin and Gold. It hints that the new foundation must be something that cannot be changed by a politician or a central banker."
