      "musicalPrompt": "[Genre: Outlaw Country]\n[Style: Americana Blues]\n[Mood: Gritty, Stoic, Heavy, Determined]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Gravelly Twang]\n[Instrumentation: Telecaster Guitar, Upright Bass, Harmonica, Kick Drum]\n[Production: Raw, Dry, Live Room Sound]\n[Structure: Stomping Rhythm, Catchy Chorus, Bluesy Solo]",
      "artPrompt": "An underwater shot looking up at the surface. The surface is turbulent and stormy. A heavy, rusted iron anchor is sinking rapidly toward the viewer, dragging a chain. The anchor is glowing slightly gold. Dark blue and gold color palette. --ar 1:1\nUnderstanding the Economics: \"Hardness\" & \"Stock-to-Flow\"\nThis song introduces the listener to the Austrian Economic concept of Hardness.\nSoft Money: Money that is easy to produce (Fiat currency). If the price goes up, the government prints more, lowering the value.\nHard Money: Money that is difficult/expensive to produce.\nGold: Hard because you have to dig it out of the ground.\nBitcoin: Hard because of the \"Difficulty Adjustment\" and the hard cap of 21 million.\n\"The Math\": The lyric \"Give me the math\" is a coded reference to the blockchain ledger, which cannot be forged or debased by political decree.\nThe Anchor: This is the psychological shift. The protagonist stops trying to chase yield in the casino (Stock Market) and decides to preserve wealth outside the system.\nReady for Track 12? Now that we have secured the money, we need to secure the Home."
