      "musicalPrompt": "[Genre: Folk Rock]\n[Style: Americana]\n[Mood: Warm, Earthy, Protective, Hopeful]\n[Vocalist: Male | Baritone | Friendly]\n[Instrumentation: Acoustic Guitar, Mandolin, Bass, Light Drum Kit, Hammond Organ]\n[Production: Organic, Warm, 1970s style]\n[Structure: Standard Verse-Chorus with a joyful solo]",
      "artPrompt": "A warm, golden-hour shot of a wooden garden gate opening into a lush vegetable garden. In the background, a modest house with solar panels and a smoking chimney. A basket of fresh vegetables sits by the gate. The feeling is safety and abundance. --ar 1:1\nUnderstanding the Economics: \"Fragility vs. Resilience\"\nThis song illustrates the concept of Fragility in systems (Nassim Taleb's influence).\nEfficiency = Fragility: Modern global trade is optimized for efficiency (Just-in-Time delivery). This makes it cheap, but fragile. One boat gets stuck in the Suez Canal, or one pandemic happens, and the shelves go empty.\nRedundancy = Resilience: Localism is optimized for resilience. It might cost more \"labor\" to grow your own tomatoes than to buy them, but if the trucks stop, you still eat.1 That \"inefficiency\" is actually your insurance policy.\n\"The Fortress\": This redefines the home not as a dormitory (where you sleep between work shifts) but as a unit of production (where you create value: food, energy, care)."
